# ZMPPI - writes X*π nicely, like "3π/4", "π", "⁻π/6" or "2π".
# Output: Str9, W = 1 if X was a fraction.  Uses U,V,W, ʟMPW.
prgmZMPNUM
If W
Then
  inString(Str9+"/","/")→U
  sub(Str9+"/",1,U-1)→Str8
  If Str8="1"
  ""→Str8
  If Str8="⁻1"
  "⁻"→Str8
  If Str8="0"
  Then
    "0"→Str9
  Else
    If U>length(Str9)
    Then
      Str8+"π"→Str9
    Else
      Str8+"π"+sub(Str9,U,length(Str9)-U+1)→Str9
    End
  End
End
